# Addify engine on the one Linux server (Ubuntu 24.04, Python 3.12, x86_64). Top-level pins.
# requirements.lock is compiled from this, holding every other package at the version the
# AWS kit's verified lock had (hosting-kit/repo/engine/requirements.lock), minus redis/boto3:
#   uv pip compile requirements.in -c <old lock, names==versions only> --python-version 3.12 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --generate-hashes -o requirements.lock
# The numerical pins are the Mac's (HOSTING-PORTABILITY.md B2): 3.12 is the one CPython where
# numpy 1.26.4 still has a wheel for both arm64 and x86_64.
